From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:13:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dts: pinephone: jack detection and LuneOS headphone widget
 naming

Two LuneOS-specific audio changes:

- Enable the analog codec's internal bias resistor. The
  allwinner,internal-bias-resistor property is still honoured by
  sound/soc/sunxi/sun50i-codec-analog.c and is needed for reliable
  headset-button detection on this board.

- LuneOS' audio configuration refers to the headphone widget as
  "Headphone", not "Headphone Jack". Rename it in widgets, routing and
  simple-audio-card,jack-pins together, so the jack-pins entry keeps
  naming a pin that exists and jack detection still binds.

The allwinner,inverted-jack-detection property the previous version of
this patch also set is gone; jack detection is now driven by the
jack-type property, which the dtsi already sets to "headset".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS userspace policy]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
index 9cbdff334ef5..7ab4fcc87a69 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
@@ -483,6 +483,7 @@ &codec {
 
 &codec_analog {
 	cpvdd-supply = <&reg_eldo1>;
+	allwinner,internal-bias-resistor;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -984,11 +985,11 @@ &sound {
 	simple-audio-card,aux-devs = <&codec_analog>, <&codec>, <&speaker_amp>;
 	simple-audio-card,widgets = "Microphone", "Headset Microphone",
 				    "Microphone", "Internal Microphone",
-				    "Headphone", "Headphone Jack",
+				    "Headphone", "Headphone",
 				    "Speaker", "Internal Earpiece",
 				    "Speaker", "Internal Speaker";
 	simple-audio-card,routing =
-			"Headphone Jack", "HP",
+			"Headphone", "HP",
 			"Internal Earpiece", "EARPIECE",
 			"Internal Speaker", "Speaker Amp OUTL",
 			"Internal Speaker", "Speaker Amp OUTR",
@@ -1003,7 +1004,7 @@ &sound {
 			"Headset Microphone", "HBIAS",
 			"MIC2", "Headset Microphone";
 	simple-audio-card,jack-pins =
-			"1c22e00.codec", "Headphone Jack",
+			"1c22e00.codec", "Headphone",
 			"1c22e00.codec", "Headset Microphone";
 	simple-audio-card,jack-pins-mask = <1>, <2>;
 
